A||||8||Fformula88||Rear Compartment Fans||||1||
Z||000000||Fformula88||02-09-2001||05:57 PM||||Did all V6 fieros have these accept the 88's?  Also, do they pull air out of the compartment or blow it in?  Finally are these things really necessary?  I cannot find ANY info on them whatsoever.  Thanx.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||02-09-2001||06:05 PM||||They blow air in across the alternator and the coil area. 88's didn't have them. Only the 85 thru 88 V-6's. Why were they there and if they helped? I don't know. Obviously in 88 they decided they weren't a benefit.<BR>I don't even know if mine works. I never checked it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||02-09-2001||06:24 PM||||I believe the 88 also has different heat shielding for the Alt. and coil...||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||02-09-2001||08:00 PM||||read my heat management article. <A HREF="http://fierocave.shorturl.com" TARGET=_blank>The Ogre's Fiero Cave</A><P>As installed they are of limited benifit. It blows air onto the coil and alt. I'm not sure where the intake for the blower is. A relativly simple modification makes the blower do the job it was really intended for.<P>do not consider removing it untill you read my article.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fformula88||02-10-2001||10:10 AM||||Good info in the cave Ogre!  I'd never really noticed it in other V6's, and was left wondering what it was in my dads new 85 SE.  Your right that it shouldn't be removed!  Every bit of cooling helps.  Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||02-11-2001||12:21 AM||||that cooling fan is inside the rt quarter panel near the right end of the rear storage trunk, I think its connected to the fan switch so it comes on when the fan does, but dont hold me to that.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||02-11-2001||02:18 AM||||Yep, it comes on when the front compartment fan does.  No seperate switch for it.  I'd like to wire the rear compartment fan to run whenever the engine is on, the way these cars eat alternators and ignition coils.  Anybody done that?   ||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||02-11-2001||06:34 AM||||id think that would be pretty ez. just a matter of cutting a wire and running it to an ignition hot.||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||02-11-2001||12:02 PM||||You have to be carefull where you tap the wire for the V6 aux fan. If you tap it in the wrong place then you effect both fans. The best spot for any modification looks to be the green control line at the aux fan relay.<P>If you look at the schematics.... making the fan come on whenever the key is on is a simple matter of cutting the green wire by the relay and grounding it. The Fan E line that provides power to this circuit is already key controlled.<P>Again.... Don't assume the deletion of the fan in 88 was a statement that they aren't needed. GM was more likely looking to cut cost. Sinse this isn't a safety item it was high on the list of things to cut.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 02-11-2001).]||||reg||1
